cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Different Sides of the Same Repository: Maintenance and Coupling in PyPI Cross-Ecosystem Packages (Replication Package)"
message: "If you use this artifact, please cite the accompanying paper and this archived dataset."
type: dataset
authors:
  - name: "Anonymous Authors"
abstract: >-
  Data tables and analysis scripts for an empirical study of 2,674 GitHub
  repositories with packages on PyPI and at least one of npm, Maven, or
  Crates.io. The artifact contains the repository population, ecosystem-side
  heuristic labels and rule-based Python-related maintenance topics
  (preliminary study), six-class maintenance-task classifications of 128,570
  maintenance artifacts (RQ1), and static evidence of build/package-time and
  potential runtime coupling for 2,250 analyzed repositories (RQ2).
keywords:
  - software ecosystem
  - repository mining
  - software maintenance
  - cross-ecosystem packages
  - PyPI
  - static analysis
license: "CC-BY-4.0"
repository-code: "https://anonymous.4open.science/r/MSR2027_Different-Sides-of-the-Same-Repository/"
date-released: "2026-10-24"
